messages:
elaine: FYI PR 1302 is up 00 0adds a compact guide for function/tool calling + a tiny JSON schema example. Need a quick docs QA: clarity, SDK snippet parity (py/js), and a short parse-fallback sample.

matt: Will take a look this afternoon. Which SDK names are you using? We changed "tools" -> "invocations" in the last API patch.

elaine: Good reminder. The prose currently uses "invocations" but the example JSON still shows "tools" (old) 0I'll update the sample. Also the schema uses nullable meta per prior discussion.

sam: Can you paste the schema here so I can validate quickly? Small teams got tripped by missing required fields last time.

elaine: Schema from the PR:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "command": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
    "meta": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "null"}]},
    "status": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ok", "error"]}
  },
  "required": ["command", "status"]
}
```

nina: Schema looks good. Suggest adding a single-sentence note: "runtime may emit extra top-level keys; parsers should avoid strict rejection." Keeps examples simple without forcing additionalProperties in sample.

matt: Agree. Also request: add a 3-line JS helper to normalize nullable meta so people copy less defensive code.

elaine: Added helper. JS snippet in PR now: 

```js
function normalizeMeta(obj) {
  return obj.meta == null ? {} : obj.meta;
}
const output = response.invocations?.[0]?.output || {};
const meta = normalizeMeta(output);
console.log(meta);
```

sam: For py snippet please use `.get("invocations", [])[0].get("output", {})` pattern and mention KeyError avoidance.

elaine: Will update. Also planning a tiny fallback example for non-JSON responses (pseudo-code) 0something like: 

```
try:
  parsed = json.loads(text)
except ValueError:
  parsed = try_regex_extract(text)
```

nina: Perfect. I ran the link-checker: one broken link to an old ticket and an internal runbook link missing. I will fix both and re-run.

doc-bot: PR 1302 markdown-lint: passed. link-check: 1 warning.

matt: +1 after the sample naming and fallback snippet are updated.

sam: +1 for schema and helper; please ensure py example shows safe access pattern.

nina: I'll push the link fixes in ~10m and then give final +1.

elaine: Thanks 0I'll wait for your push then merge today. I'll add a short changelog entry and a link to the SDK snippet sandbox after landing. :tada:
